def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(127, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"OBSERVE THE MONTH OF AVIV" (16:1) — OBSERVE THE MONTH NEAR TO AVIV, SO THAT AVIV FALLS IN ITS SEASON. The head row of piska 127 ({SP_(127, 1, "שמור", "את", "החדש", "סמוך", "לאביב")} "observe the month near to Aviv"; {SP_(127, 1, "שיהא", "בזמנו")} "that it be in its season"): THE INTERCALATION READ OUT OF "OBSERVE" — the month before Nisan watched so that the spring month keeps its season: the calendar\'s leap month a LAW OF THIS VERSE (the compile: the year clock\'s intercalation parameter, Mishnah Sanhedrin 1:2 / Rosh Hashanah 7a the exam). Fresh.')
srow(127, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT IT BE THAT IF THE YEAR IS SHORT BY FOURTEEN OR FIFTEEN DAYS YOU GIVE IT FOURTEEN OR FIFTEEN DAYS? THE TEACHING SAYS "MONTH" — NOT LESS AND NOT MORE. ({SP_(127, 2, "ארבעה", "עשר", "יום", "או", "חמשה", "עשר", "יום")} "fourteen days or fifteen days"; {SP_(127, 2, "לא", "פחות", "ולא", "יתר")} "not less and not more"): THE LEAP\'S UNIT A WHOLE MONTH — never a fortnight; the parameter\'s grain. Fresh.')
srow(127, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT IT BE THAT IF THE YEAR IS SHORT BY FORTY OR FIFTY DAYS YOU GIVE IT FORTY OR FIFTY DAYS? THE TEACHING SAYS "MONTH" — NOT LESS AND NOT MORE. ({SP_(127, 3, "ארבעים", "יום", "או", "חמשים", "יום")} "forty days or fifty days"): the other bound — never two months at once; the English\'s note Tosefta Sanhedrin 2:7-8. Fresh.')
srow(127, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"OBSERVE THE MONTH OF AVIV" — IN THREE PLACES SCRIPTURE RECALLS THE FESTIVALS\' SECTION: IN THE PRIESTS\' TORAH FOR THEIR ORDER, ({SP_(127, 4, "בשלשה", "מקומות", "מזכיר", "פרשת", "מועדות")} "in three places it recalls the festivals\' section"; {SP_(127, 4, "בתורת", "כהנים", "מפני", "סדרן")} "in the Priests\' Torah for their order"): THE SHELF\'S OWN MAP OF THE KIN — Leviticus 23 (the order), read at its sitting (lev_23_festivals, credited by name); this row and the two after it the reason the chapter restates the calendar. Fresh.')
srow(127, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'IN THE BOOK OF THE NUMBERED FOR THE OFFERING, ({SP_(127, 5, "בחומש", "הפקודים", "מפני", "קרבן")} "in the book of the numbered for the offering"): Numbers 28-29 (the English names 9:1-14) — the offerings, read at their sittings (num_28, num_29, num_09 credited by name). Fresh.')
srow(127, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'IN THE REPETITION OF THE TORAH FOR THE INTERCALATION. ({SP_(127, 6, "במשנה", "תורה", "מפני", "העבור")} "in the repetition of the Torah for the intercalation"): THIS CHAPTER\'S REASON NAMED — the calendar restated here FOR THE LEAP MONTH (127:1-3): the compile\'s new parameter is what the chapter adds to Leviticus 23; the kin\'s cells reused, the intercalation new. Fresh.')
srow(127, 7, 'CONTEXT', f'TO TEACH THAT MOSES HEARD THE FESTIVALS\' SECTION AND SAID IT TO ISRAEL, AND REPEATED IT TO THEM AT THE TIME OF THE DEED. The row without a citation ({SP_(127, 7, "וחזר", "ושנאה", "להם", "בשעת", "מעשה")} "and repeated it to them at the time of the deed"): the retelling\'s reason — a law re-said when its season comes. Fresh.')
srow(127, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: HE TOLD THEM THE LAWS OF PASSOVER AT PASSOVER, OF THE ASSEMBLY AT THE ASSEMBLY, OF THE FEAST AT THE FEAST; FROM HERE THEY SAID: MOSES WARNED ISRAEL TO STUDY THE MATTER AND EXPOUND IT. ({SP_(127, 8, "הלכות", "הפסח", "בפסח")} "the laws of Passover at Passover"; {SP_(127, 8, "שונים", "בענין", "ודורשים", "בו")} "studying the matter and expounding it"): the shelf\'s name for the feast of weeks is THE ASSEMBLY (Atzeret) and for booths THE FEAST bare — the three names the compile\'s labels; Tosefta Megillah 4:5 the English\'s note. Fresh.')
srow(128, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL MAKE THE PASSOVER" (16:1) — THAT ITS MAKING BE FOR THE NAME OF THE PASSOVER; IF HE SLAUGHTERED IT NOT FOR ITS NAME, IT IS DISQUALIFIED. The head row of piska 128 ({SP_(128, 1, "שתהא", "עשיתו", "לשם", "פסח")} "that its making be for the name of Passover"; {SP_(128, 1, "שלא", "לשמו", "פסול")} "not for its name — disqualified"): THE INTENTION CLAUSE — the Passover offered under another name void (Mishnah Zevachim 1:1, Pesachim 5:2 the exam): the compile\'s cell carries the offering\'s NAME as a parameter of its validity. Fresh.')
srow(128, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'I HAVE ONLY ITS SLAUGHTER; WHENCE TO INCLUDE THE RECEIVING AND THE SPRINKLING OF ITS BLOOD? "AND YOU SHALL MAKE". MIGHT I INCLUDE ITS ROASTING AND THE RINSING OF ITS ENTRAILS? "AND YOU SHALL SLAUGHTER" (16:2) — SLAUGHTER WAS IN THE GENERAL RULE AND WENT OUT TO TEACH: AS SLAUGHTER IS FOR THE NAME OF SERVICE, SO ONLY WHAT IS SERVICE. ({SP_(128, 2, "קבול", "דמו", "וזריקת", "דמו")} "the receiving of its blood and the sprinkling of its blood"; {SP_(128, 2, "זביחה", "בכלל", "היתה", "ולמה", "יצאה")} "slaughter was in the general rule, and why did it go out"): I8\'s SHAPE (the particular singled out to teach the class, named without a code) — the four services (slaughter, receiving, carrying, sprinkling) take the name; roasting and rinsing do not; Mishnah Zevachim 2:3 the English\'s note. Fresh.')
srow(128, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"TO THE LORD YOUR GOD" — TO THE UNIQUE NAME. ({SP_(128, 3, "לשם", "המיחד")} "to the unique Name"): the name the offering is made for is the Name. Fresh.')
srow(128, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"FOR IN THE MONTH OF AVIV" — A MONTH THAT IS FIT: NOT HOT AND NOT COLD; AND SO IT SAYS "HE BRINGS OUT PRISONERS INTO PROSPERITY" (PSALM 68:7). ({SP_(128, 4, "חדש", "שהוא", "כשר", "לא", "חם", "ולא", "צונן")} "a month that is fit: not hot and not cold"): the spring month\'s fitness — the Psalm\'s word played on "fit" (the English\'s note). Fresh.')
srow(128, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE LORD YOUR GOD BROUGHT YOU OUT OF EGYPT BY NIGHT" — AND DID THEY GO OUT BY NIGHT? DID THEY NOT GO OUT BY DAY, AS IT IS SAID "ON THE MORROW OF THE PASSOVER" (NUMBERS 33:3)? IT TEACHES THAT THEY WERE REDEEMED BY NIGHT. ({SP_(128, 5, "וכי", "בלילה", "יצאו")} "and did they go out by night"; {SP_(128, 5, "שנגאלו", "בלילה")} "that they were redeemed by night"): TWO VERSES ON THE EXODUS\'S HOUR upheld by dividing the redemption (the night) from the going out (the day) — the tape\'s own lines at Exodus 12 (the night\'s marker) and Numbers 33:3 (the day\'s) read together; Onkelos\'s addition "and He did miracles for you at night" the same reading. Fresh.')
srow(129, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL SLAUGHTER THE PASSOVER" (16:2) — THAT ITS SLAUGHTER BE FOR THE NAME OF THE PASSOVER; IF HE SLAUGHTERED IT NOT FOR ITS NAME, IT IS DISQUALIFIED. The head row of piska 129 ({SP_(129, 1, "שתהא", "שחיטתו", "לשם", "פסח")} "that its slaughter be for the name of Passover"): 128:1 said again at 16:2\'s verb — the piska\'s twin opening (the English\'s note). Fresh.')
srow(129, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'I HAVE ONLY ITS SLAUGHTER; WHENCE TO INCLUDE THE RECEIVING AND SPRINKLING OF ITS BLOOD? "AND YOU SHALL MAKE" (16:1). ({SP_(129, 2, "מנין", "לרבות", "קבול", "דמו")} "whence to include the receiving of its blood"): 128:2\'s first step repeated. Fresh.')
srow(129, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'MIGHT I INCLUDE THE BURNING OF ITS FATS? THE TEACHING SAYS "AND YOU SHALL SLAUGHTER". ({SP_(129, 3, "הקטר", "חלביו")} "the burning of its fats"): the excluded service here the fats, not the roasting. Fresh.')
srow(129, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'SLAUGHTER WAS IN THE GENERAL RULE AND WENT OUT TO TEACH: AS SLAUGHTER IS PARTICULAR IN THAT IT HINDERS ATONEMENT, SO ALL THAT HINDERS ATONEMENT; THE BURNING OF THE FATS WENT OUT, WHICH DOES NOT HINDER ATONEMENT. The row without a citation ({SP_(129, 4, "שמעכבת", "את", "הכפרה")} "that hinders the atonement"; {SP_(129, 4, "יצאה", "הקטרה")} "the burning went out"): I8\'s shape a second time with a different FEATURE — atonement-hindering, not service-for-the-name: the two piskaot draw the same line by two features (the compile\'s validity set the four blood services). Fresh.')
srow(129, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"TO THE LORD YOUR GOD" — TO THE UNIQUE NAME. ({SP_(129, 5, "לשם", "המיחד")} "to the unique Name"): 128:3 again. Fresh.')
srow(129, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"FLOCK AND HERD" — BUT DOES THE PASSOVER NOT COME ONLY FROM THE SHEEP AND THE GOATS? WHY THEN "FLOCK AND HERD"? FLOCK FOR THE PASSOVER AND HERD FOR THE FESTIVAL OFFERING. ANOTHER WORD: TO COMPARE ALL THAT COMES FROM FLOCK AND HERD TO THE PASSOVER — AS THE PASSOVER, AN OBLIGATION, COMES ONLY FROM UNCONSECRATED BEASTS, SO EVERY OBLIGATION. ({SP_(129, 6, "צאן", "לפסח", "ובקר", "לחגיגה")} "flock for the Passover and herd for the festival offering"; {SP_(129, 6, "אינו", "בא", "אלא", "מן", "החלין")} "comes only from the unconsecrated"): THE HERD READ AS THE FESTIVAL OFFERING (chagigah) — Exodus 12:5\'s lamb upheld, 16:2\'s herd a second offering; ONKELOS WRITES THE SAME LAW ("the holy slaughterings from the oxen", asserted); the second reading Mishnah Menachot 7:6 (the English\'s note) — an obligation from unconsecrated stock: the compile\'s source parameter. Fresh.')
srow(129, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN THE PLACE WHICH THE LORD WILL CHOOSE TO MAKE HIS NAME DWELL THERE" — THIS IS SHILOH AND THE ETERNAL HOUSE. ({SP_(129, 7, "זו", "שילה", "ובית", "עולמים")} "this is Shiloh and the eternal house"): THE PLACE\'S TWO STATIONS at the Passover\'s verse — chapter 12\'s eras table (high_places_banned, the stations by call) the cell the compile reuses; 74:2 the English\'s pointer (chapter 12\'s sitting). Fresh.')
srow(130, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT EAT LEAVEN WITH IT" (16:3) — R. JUDAH SAYS: WHENCE THAT ONE WHO EATS LEAVEN FROM THE SIXTH HOUR ONWARD TRANSGRESSES A PROHIBITION? THE TEACHING SAYS "YOU SHALL NOT EAT LEAVEN WITH IT". The head row of piska 130 ({SP_(130, 1, "משש", "שעות", "ולמעלה")} "from six hours onward"): THE BAN\'S ONSET ON THE EVE — the sixth hour of the fourteenth, "with it" read as the Passover\'s slaughter-time (Mishnah Pesachim 1:4-5 the exam; Pesachim 28b the segment if disputed): the compile\'s clock parameter for the leaven ban. Fresh.')
srow(130, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SIMEON SAID: CAN IT BE SO? THE TEACHING SAYS "YOU SHALL NOT EAT LEAVEN WITH IT, SEVEN DAYS YOU SHALL EAT UNLEAVENED BREAD WITH IT" — WHEN HE IS UNDER "ARISE, EAT UNLEAVENED BREAD" HE IS UNDER "DO NOT EAT LEAVEN"; WHEN NOT, NOT. ({SP_(130, 2, "בקום", "אכל", "מצה")} "under arise, eat unleavened bread"; {SP_(130, 2, "בבל", "תאכל", "חמץ")} "under do not eat leaven"): THE DISPUTE — the ban bound to the positive command\'s onset (nightfall), R. Judah\'s sixth hour refused: the parameter has two arms; Pesachim 28b the segment. Fresh.')
srow(130, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"BREAD OF AFFLICTION" — TO THE EXCLUSION OF SCALDED BREAD AND CAKES. ({SP_(130, 3, "פרט", "לחלוט", "ולאשישה")} "to the exclusion of scalded bread and cakes"): the bread\'s kind narrowed by "affliction" (Mishnah Pesachim 2:6 the exam; the one seat of the phrase in the Bible, asserted). Fresh.')
srow(130, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT A MAN NOT FULFIL HIS DUTY WITH COARSE BREAD? THE TEACHING SAYS "UNLEAVENED BREAD" — EVEN LIKE SOLOMON\'S. IF SO WHY "BREAD OF AFFLICTION"? TO EXCLUDE SCALDED BREAD AND CAKES. ({SP_(130, 4, "בפת", "הדראה")} "with coarse bread"; {SP_(130, 4, "כמצה", "של", "שלמה")} "like Solomon\'s unleavened bread"): the two bounds — the coarse in, the rich out. Fresh.')
srow(130, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'R. SIMEON SAYS: WHY IS IT CALLED BREAD OF AFFLICTION? FOR THE AFFLICTION THEY SUFFERED IN EGYPT. The row without a citation ({SP_(130, 5, "על", "שם", "ענוי", "שנתענו", "במצרים")} "for the affliction they were afflicted in Egypt"): the name\'s reason. Fresh.')
srow(130, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR IN HASTE YOU WENT OUT OF THE LAND OF EGYPT" — MIGHT THE HASTE BE ISRAEL\'S AND EGYPT\'S? THE TEACHING SAYS "AGAINST ANY OF THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL NOT A DOG SHALL MOVE ITS TONGUE" (EXODUS 11:7): EGYPT\'S WAS THE HASTE, NOT ISRAEL\'S. ({SP_(130, 6, "למצרים", "היה", "חפזון")} "Egypt had the haste"; {SP_(130, 6, "ולא", "היה", "חפזון", "לישראל")} "and Israel had no haste"): "IN HASTE" three in the Bible (Exodus 12:11, here, Isaiah 52:12 "not in haste" — asserted): the haste assigned to Egypt from the dog\'s silence — the narrative\'s line reread as the law\'s reason. Fresh.')
srow(130, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT YOU MAY REMEMBER THE DAY OF YOUR GOING OUT OF EGYPT ALL THE DAYS OF YOUR LIFE" — R. ELEAZAR BEN AZARIAH: I AM LIKE SEVENTY YEARS OLD AND NEVER MERITED THAT THE EXODUS BE SAID AT NIGHT UNTIL BEN ZOMA EXPOUNDED: "THE DAYS OF YOUR LIFE" — THE DAYS; "ALL THE DAYS" — THE NIGHTS. THE SAGES: THIS WORLD; "ALL" — THE DAYS OF THE MESSIAH. ({SP_(130, 7, "הריני", "כבן", "שבעים", "שנה")} "behold I am like seventy years old"; {SP_(130, 7, "כל", "ימי", "חייך", "הלילות")} "all the days of your life — the nights"): THE MISHNAH INSIDE THE SPINE (Berakhot 1:5 — the English\'s note; the Haggadah\'s row): "all" read twice — the nights, or the Messiah\'s days: the remembrance effect\'s schedule a two-arm parameter (daily, day and night). Fresh.')
srow(131, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"NO LEAVEN SHALL BE SEEN TO YOU" (16:4) — YOU MAY SEE OTHERS\'; NOT SEEN TO YOU — YOU MAY SEE THE MOST HIGH\'S; NOT SEEN TO YOU — YOU MAY SEE IT IN THE SQUARE. The head row of piska 131 ({SP_(131, 1, "רואה", "אתה", "לאחרים")} "you may see others\'"; {SP_(131, 1, "רואה", "אתה", "בפלטיא")} "you may see it in the square"): "TO YOU" THREE EXCLUSIONS — a gentile\'s, the sanctuary\'s, the ownerless: the ban\'s object the owned leaven (the compile\'s ownership parameter; Pesachim 5b the segment if needed). Fresh.')
srow(131, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"NO LEAVEN SHALL BE SEEN TO YOU" — NULLIFY IT IN YOUR HEART. FROM HERE THEY SAID (MISHNAH PESACHIM 3:7): ONE GOING TO SLAUGHTER HIS PASSOVER OR CIRCUMCISE HIS SON WHO REMEMBERS LEAVEN IN HIS HOUSE — IF HE CAN RETURN AND REMOVE IT AND RETURN TO HIS COMMANDMENT, LET HIM RETURN; IF NOT, LET HIM NULLIFY IT IN HIS HEART. ({SP_(131, 2, "בטל", "בלבך")} "nullify it in your heart"; {SP_(131, 2, "ואם", "לאו", "יבטל", "בלבו")} "and if not, let him nullify it in his heart"): THE MISHNAH CITED IN THE HEBREW ITSELF — nullification a second way of removal; the exam\'s row. Fresh.')
srow(131, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"NO LEAVEN SHALL BE SEEN TO YOU" (EXODUS 13:7) AND "NO LEAVENING AGENT SHALL BE SEEN TO YOU" (16:4) — THIS IS THE DIVISION BETWEEN THE HOUSE OF SHAMMAI AND THE HOUSE OF HILLEL (MISHNAH BEITZAH 1:1): SHAMMAI, LEAVENING AN OLIVE AND LEAVEN A DATE; HILLEL, BOTH AN OLIVE. ({SP_(131, 3, "בית", "שמיי", "אומרים", "שאור", "כזית", "וחמץ", "ככותבת")} "the House of Shammai say: leavening an olive and leaven a date"): THE TWO WORDS TWO MEASURES — Exodus 13:7\'s six tokens shared in order with 16:4 (asserted) and the one word that differs the dispute\'s ground; the Mishnah cited in the Hebrew itself. Fresh.')
srow(131, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"NONE OF THE FLESH YOU SLAUGHTER AT EVENING SHALL REMAIN OVERNIGHT" — WHAT SLAUGHTER DO YOU SLAUGHTER TO EAT AT EVENING? SAY: THIS IS THE PASSOVER. ({SP_(131, 4, "איזו", "זביחה", "אתה", "זובח")} "what slaughter do you slaughter"; {SP_(131, 4, "הוי", "אומר", "זה", "הפסח")} "say, this is the Passover"): the night\'s flesh the Passover\'s — Exodus 12:10\'s "leave none until morning" the kin (asserted nothing shared in order — the same law in new words). Fresh.')
srow(131, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"ON THE FIRST DAY UNTIL MORNING" — THE MORNING OF THE THIRD, OR MIGHT IT BE THE SECOND\'S? THE TEACHING SAYS "VOW" (LEVITICUS 7:16 "IF A VOW"), "FREEWILL" ("OR A FREEWILL OFFERING") — TO INCLUDE THE FESTIVAL OFFERING THAT COMES WITH THE PASSOVER, EATEN TWO DAYS. HOW THEN "UNTIL MORNING"? THE THIRD\'S MORNING. ({SP_(131, 5, "לבקרו", "של", "שלישי")} "until the morning of the third"; {SP_(131, 5, "לרבות", "חגיגה", "הבאה", "עם", "הפסח")} "to include the festival offering that comes with the Passover"): THE FESTIVAL OFFERING OF THE FOURTEENTH GIVEN TWO DAYS by the peace offering\'s law (Leviticus 7:16-17, the kin\'s ledger) — 16:4\'s "morning" split from the Passover\'s: the compile\'s two eating windows (the Passover one night, its chagigah two days). Fresh.')
